# Secrets — never commit
.env
*/.env
**/.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*/.venv/
**/.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Caches / build artifacts
.pytest_cache/
**/.cache/
**/hf_cache/
**/model_cache/
**/*.faiss
**/*.index
**/corpus_cache/

# Built indexes are normally artifacts — reproducible from `retrieval.build_index` — and
# stay out of git. The *deployed* version's is the deliberate exception: baking it during a
# Docker build takes ~48 minutes on a 2-core builder (build_parallelism drops to 1 worker),
# which risks the build timeout. Shipping the 38MB index turns that into a file copy.
#
# V9.0 and V10.0 both carry one because the deployment moved from V9.0 to V10.0 and V9.0 is
# kept deployable as a rollback target. The two copies are byte-identical, so git stores the
# blobs once — the second version costs tree entries, not 38MB. Every other version's index
# remains ignored.
**/index_store/
!V9.0/index_store/
!V9.0/index_store/**
!V10.0/index_store/
!V10.0/index_store/**
**/index_store_dev/
**/build_full.log

# Local dev server log
**/server.log

# local run artifacts
.cloudflared.exe
serve.log
app.log
tunnel.log

# Timestamped benchmark runs — only results_latest.json is referenced; the rest are
# snapshots of individual runs that go stale and start contradicting the README.
**/benchmarks/results_2*.json
**/benchmarks/results_full_pipeline.json

# Generated audio (TTS output). audio_samples/tts_hi.wav is kept deliberately as the
# fixture the STT verification command uses.
**/audio_samples/answer_*.wav

# Working docs kept locally, deliberately not shipped. The repo carries CHANGELOG.md,
# a root README, and the per-version docs inside V*/ — root-level duplicates of those
# only created two files disagreeing about the same thing.
/DECISIONS.md
/DEPLOY.md
/HANDOFF.md
/render.yaml
